{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"Before editing, here’s the concrete plan I’m applying:\n\n- In `id_stage`, reset/flush/invalid fetch will clear only `valid` and `ctrl`; the PC, register values, immediate, instruction, and register indexes keep their previous/don’t-care values.\n- In `ex_stage`, reset and DIV/REM busy bubbles will clear only `valid`, `ctrl`, and the tiny branch-control bit that could otherwise look meaningful; the ALU/result payload stays off the zero arm.\n- In `mem_stage`, dmem-stall keeps the forwarding hold behavior, while reset and true bubbles clear `valid` and `ctrl` so stale MEM/WB data cannot be forwarded or written."}}
