{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Replicate GPR read banks\n========================\n\nWhat changed\n------------\n- Replaced the single `regs[0:31]` array in `rtl/reg_file.sv` with two\n  identical banks, `regs_rs1` and `regs_rs2`.\n- Reset writes both banks to zero and architectural writes update both banks\n  in the same clock edge.\n- Kept x0 hardwiring and same-cycle write-first bypass independently on each\n  read port.\n- Added conservative `keep`, `syn_keep`, and `dont_touch` attributes to the\n  duplicate storage arrays to discourage synthesis from merging the banks.\n- Extended `test/test_reg_file.py` so reset, ordinary writes, x0 writes, and\n  write-first bypass are checked through both read ports, including independent\n  rs1/rs2 read addresses.\n\nDeviations\n----------\n- No pipeline, forwarding, RVFI, or memory-side behavior was changed.\n\nConcerns\n--------\n- The synthesis attributes are intentionally conservative. Verilator accepts\n  them, but the exact Gowin mapping choice is left to the vendor flow.\n\nLocal status\n------------\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass.\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py`: pass.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench`: build failed before simulation because this\n  direct Makefile path defaulted the harness to `NRET=2` while `cores/bench`\n  declares `nret: 1`.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, 2 ELFs tested.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
