{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Implementation Notes\n\n## What changed\n\n- Kept `ALU_MUL` combinational in `rtl/alu.sv`, but reduced it to a low-half 32-bit multiply result.\n- Removed real `MULH`/`MULHU`/`MULHSU` high-half product generation from the non-ALTOPS ALU path. The ALTOPS substitutions remain present in `alu.sv`.\n- Added `rtl/mulh_unit.sv`, a 32-cycle shift-add high-half multiplier with signedness handling for `MULH`, `MULHU`, and `MULHSU`. Its ALTOPS mode returns the same substituted formulas used by riscv-formal.\n- Updated `rtl/ex_stage.sv` to start `mulh_unit` for high-half multiply ops, fold it into the existing long-stall behavior, preserve operands at start, and capture the completed result once into EX/MEM.\n- Adjusted `test/test_alu.py` so ALU unit coverage now targets RV32I plus single-cycle low-half `MUL`.\n- Added `test/test_mulh_unit.py` with signed, unsigned, mixed-signedness, corner, and back-to-back high-half multiply vectors.\n\n## Deviations\n\n- I mirrored the existing `mdiv_unit`/EX pending-result pattern instead of making a shared generic long-op wrapper. That keeps the change scoped and avoids reshaping pipeline control.\n\n## Concerns\n\n- High-half multiply latency is now 32 shift-add steps plus the existing EX accept cycle. This matches the hypothesis tradeoff: rare `MULH*` instructions stall longer so the hot ALU cone can drop the 33x33 high-product muxing.\n- A bare `make cosim TARGET=bench` in this checkout builds the harness with the script default `NRET=2` and fails before simulation because this core is `nret: 1`. Rerunning as `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` uses the correct single-issue port set and passed.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass.\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_alu.py cores/bench/test/test_mulh_unit.py`: pass, 2 passed.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, `{\"passed\": true, \"elfs_tested\": 2}`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
