{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"One subtlety I’m accounting for before touching files: some producers can later suppress their write because of a misaligned jump or memory trap. The registered select removes the compare path, but EX still needs a tiny “is that forwarded stage actually writing?” guard so a stale select does not manufacture a value after a trap."}}
