{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"agent_message","text":"The counterexample is clear: EX0 fired a redirect while EX1 was held, so the frontend jumped, but the branch payload was not accepted into EX1 that cycle. When it later advanced, its recorded `pc_next` was linear, so wrong-path instructions retired before the target. I’m gating redirects to cycles where EX0 is actually accepted by the EX1 register."}}
