{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --stat -- cores/bench/rtl/core.sv cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv && test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" cores/bench/rtl/core.sv        | 18 +++++++++++++++++-\n cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv    | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--\n cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv | 11 +++++++++--\n cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv    | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++++---\n cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv    | 22 ++++++++++++++--------\n 5 files changed, 82 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)\n# ID-Registered Target Prefetch Predictor\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added a narrow registered prediction sideband in `id_stage.sv`: valid plus `pc+imm` target for legal aligned direct JALs and backward conditional branches.\n- Wired the sideband through `core.sv` into EX/IF/hazard logic without changing top-level IO or widening the ID/EX payload.\n- Updated `ex_stage.sv` to confirm registered target predictions against resolved direct JAL/branch outcomes. A predicted but not-taken conditional branch redirects back to `pc+4` because IF spent that cycle fetching the predicted target.\n- Updated `if_stage.sv` to drive `io_imemAddr` from the registered predicted target for the speculative slot, accept it only on the hazard-approved confirm handshake, and otherwise use the existing redirect/sequential PC behavior.\n- Updated `hazard_unit.sv` so prediction acceptance is gated by imem readiness, dmem hold, and long-DIV hold; accepted predictions suppress the redirect bubble.\n\n## Deviations\n\n- I did not add directed cocotb tests in this iteration. The change is covered locally by lint, riscv-formal, and full cosim.\n- The sideband is kept as discrete signals rather than a new typedef or ID/EX field, matching the hypothesis goal of avoiding extra payload width on the hot pipe bundle.\n\n## Concerns\n\n- The accept path still feeds IF valid/PC control from EX confirmation plus hazard gating, so the Fmax benefit depends on whether removing the EX target add from the fetch-address path is enough to offset the new control muxing.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench` defaults the harness to `NRET=2` in this checkout and fails to compile this `nret: 1` core. Rerunning with `NRET=1` matches `cores/bench/core.yaml` and passes.\n\n## Local status\n\n- Lint: pass\n  `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`\n- Formal: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed\n  `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`\n- Cosim: pass, 2 ELFs tested\n  `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
