{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_80","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Prechecked redirect-fill BTIC implementation notes\n\nWhat changed:\n- Added `branch_fill_predictor.sv`, a two-entry direct-control-flow BTIC with\n  combinational ID prelookup, registered ID/EX hit/instruction sideband, and a\n  single pending miss-fill slot.\n- Added ID/EX sideband fields for the ID-computed direct target, target+4,\n  BTIC hit, and cached instruction in both package declaration files.\n- ID now computes direct branch/JAL targets and drives BTIC prelookup only for\n  valid non-JALR direct control-flow instructions.\n- EX uses the registered direct target for branch/JAL redirects, keeps JALR on\n  the rs1-based fallback path, emits cached-fill candidates on aligned taken\n  direct redirects, and trains the BTIC only on sideband misses.\n- IF can inject a cached target instruction during an accepted redirect and\n  advances the fetch PC to the precomputed target+4.\n- Hazard suppresses the normal redirect bubble only for an accepted cached fill\n  and keeps dmem/long-DIV fallback behavior unchanged.\n- Updated the core cocotb source list so tests build the new predictor module.\n\nDeviations:\n- Implemented a two-entry fully associative BTIC rather than a one-entry table.\n- Did not add a separate `test_prechecked_btic.py`; existing pipeline tests\n  still run with the new module, and correctness was checked with formal/cosim.\n\nConcerns:\n- The BTIC assumes immutable instruction memory, matching the hypothesis and\n  benchmark environment.\n- Plain `make cosim TARGET=bench` in this checkout defaults the C++ harness to\n  `NRET=2`, while `cores/bench/core.yaml` declares `nret: 1`; the matching\n  local cosim command is `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`.\n\nLocal verification:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass.\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py`: pass.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass,\n  53 passed / 0 failed after fixing a Yosys structural loop in the first BTIC\n  fill implementation.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, 2 ELFs tested.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
