{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'rg -n \"fold|redirect|direct_target|sideband|pc_next|branch_target\" cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/test cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Static loop branch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current five-stage pipeline fetches linearly and redirects only after EX\\nresolves a taken branch or jump. CoreMark has many loop backedges, so the core\\nrepeatedly pays taken-branch flush bubbles even though those branches are easy\\nto predict from their immediate direction. The existing critical path is in the\\nEX ALU/forwarding logic, so a very small IF-side predictor has a chance to\\nimprove iterations per cycle without materially changing Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current five-stage pipeline fetches linearly and redirects only after EX\\nresolves a taken branch or jump. CoreMark has many loop backedges, so the core\\nrepeatedly pays taken-branch flush bubbles even though those branches are easy\\nto predict from their immediate direction. The existing critical path is in the\\nEX ALU/forwarding logic, so a very small IF-side predictor has a chance to\\nimprove iterations per cycle without materially changing Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a static control-flow predictor in IF: predict direct JAL as taken, predict\\nconditional branches with negative B-immediates as taken, and predict forward\\nconditional branches plus JALR as not taken. Carry the predicted next PC through\\nIF/ID and ID/EX, then have EX redirect and flush only when the resolved next PC\\ndiffers from the prediction. This should remove most loop-backedge penalties in\\nCoreMark while keeping predictor cost to a few immediate-decode gates and one\\nextra next-PC field in the pipeline payload.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted next-PC fields to IF/ID and ID/EX payloads so branch recovery can compare prediction versus resolved next PC.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode fetched direct control-flow opcodes in IF, compute B/J immediates, and advance the PC to the pr\n…[166012 of 169084 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:61c2b6a8c6d84c72]…\n/bench/rtl/00_core_pkg_first.sv:85:    logic [31:0] pc_next;\ncores/bench/rtl/00_core_pkg_first.sv:87:    logic [31:0] branch_target;\ncores/bench/rtl/00_core_pkg_first.sv:102:    logic [31:0] pc_next;\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv:20://                 redirect).\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv:85:  // EX redirect\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv:86:  logic        redirect;\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv:87:  logic [31:0] redirect_target;\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv:103:    .redirect        (redirect),\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv:104:    .redirect_target (redirect_target),\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv:149:    .redirect        (redirect),\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv:150:    .redirect_target (redirect_target)\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv:183:    .redirect       (redirect),\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv:237:    io_rvfi_pc_wdata_0  = mem_wb_w.pc_next;\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv:105:    logic [31:0] pc_next;        // resolved next-PC (target / pc+4)\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv:107:    logic [31:0] branch_target;\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv:123:    logic [31:0] pc_next;\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
