{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The experiment log confirms the thing this hypothesis is reacting to: the prior BTIC-style attempt dragged `redirect_fill_accept` back into a wide ID-side target register. I’m narrowing this to a no-cache redirect fold: compute target in ID, carry it as a separate sideband valid/data pair, and let the payload itself stay lean."}}
