{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_79","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the flush-free direct fold sideband in `cores/bench/rtl` and added directed coverage in `cores/bench/test/test_direct_fold_sideband.py`.\n\nWhat changed:\n- ID computes direct branch/JAL `pc+imm` into a separate sideband target register.\n- Only the sideband valid bit is killed on bubbles/non-accepted redirects.\n- EX uses the sideband for aligned taken direct branches/JALs, with JALR still on the conservative path.\n- IF accepts folded target instructions and advances PC to `target+4`.\n- Hazard suppresses the redirect bubble only for accepted folds.\n\nChecks passed:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_direct_fold_sideband.py`\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py`\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`\n\nWrote notes at `cores/bench/implementation_notes.md`."}}
