{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_69","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Static loop branch predictor implementation notes\n\nWhat changed:\n- Added `pred_pc_next` to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads.\n- IF now decodes direct JAL and conditional branch opcodes from the fetched\n  instruction. JAL predicts taken. Valid conditional branches with negative\n  B-immediates predict taken. Forward branches and JALR predict not taken.\n- ID latches the predicted next PC into ID/EX.\n- EX computes the resolved next PC and redirects only when it differs from the\n  carried prediction.\n- Added `rtl/00_core_pkg.sv`, a source-order shim that includes `core_pkg.sv`\n  first for shell-glob lint/build source lists. It has no hardware content.\n\nDeviations:\n- The IF branch predictor checks branch funct3 validity before predicting a\n  branch taken, matching the decoder's reserved-branch handling.\n- Predicted taken targets are required to be word-aligned. Misaligned branch\n  or jump targets therefore remain on the linear path until EX marks the\n  retiring control-flow instruction as a trap.\n\nConcerns:\n- The predictor adds immediate decode and a target add in IF, so timing should\n  be checked by the vendor flow. I did not run `make timing TARGET=bench`.\n\nLocal checks:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`\n  passed.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh` passed:\n  53 passed, 0 failed.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench` initially built the harness with its default\n  `NRET=2` and failed because this core declares `nret: 1`; rerunning as\n  `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed both tested ELFs.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
