{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Single-entry loop target predictor implementation\n\nWhat changed:\n- Added predicted_taken and predicted_next_pc metadata to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles, mirrored in 00_core_pkg_first.sv.\n- Added rtl/loop_predictor.sv: one valid entry containing a learned branch PC and target.\n- IF now selects the learned target on predictor hit and carries the prediction metadata with the fetched instruction.\n- ID latches prediction metadata into ID/EX and clears it naturally on bubbles/flushes via the existing zeroing path.\n- EX now computes the resolved next PC and redirects only when it differs from the carried prediction. It trains the predictor only for valid resolved conditional branches that are taken to a lower 4-byte-aligned target.\n- core.sv wires predictor lookup and EX training without changing the nret=1 top-level IO.\n\nDeviations:\n- None from the core hypothesis. The predictor is a single learned entry with no IF-side immediate decode, no counters, no RAM, and no RAS path.\n\nConcerns:\n- The direct `make cosim TARGET=bench` path built the harness with its default `NRET=2`, which does not match this core's `nret: 1` IO and fails in C++ compilation before running RTL. Rerunning with `NRET=1` matches the orchestrator's cosim environment and passes.\n\nLocal status:\n- Lint: pass (`verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`).\n- Formal: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`).\n- Cosim: pass (`NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`, 2 ELFs tested).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
