{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"One extra nuance showed up: false raw-source matches still drive the EX forwarding muxes, so even when the instruction does not architecturally consume a source, the retired RVFI raw-source value can be overwritten with the load address unless the trace path has an exact fix. That matches why a hazard-only IPC cleanup can fail in cosim with stalls."}}
