h the EX\\noperand muxes into the ALU and reaches about 150 logic levels. The current\\nALU contains fully combinational RV32M divide and remainder operators, so even\\nordinary forwarded ADD/load-address operations share timing with the largest\\narithmetic cone. Removing the divider from the single-cycle EX path should\\nraise Fmax by far more than the acceptance threshold, while CoreMark is\\nexpected to execute few or no DIV/REM instructions in the measured\n…[33891 of 36963 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0412d1c6598e5a98]…\n uses the fast_sum path in EX.\\n\\nConcerns:\\n- The added simple_add mux is intentionally small, but final benefit depends on Gowin's flattening and whether the new select is placed off the prior broad ALU result cone.\\n\\nLocal checks:\\n- Verilator lint passed:\\n  verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv\\n- Formal passed with the nret=1 auto-detected wrapper:\\n  RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh\\n  Result: Formal: 53 passed, 0 failed.\\n- Cosim passed with NRET=1, matching cores/bench/core.yaml:\\n  NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench\\n  Result: {\\\"passed\\\": true, \\\"elfs_tested\\\": 2}\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T05:02:21.833610Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-001-r3s0 (regression, -0.97%): After DIV/REM leave the ALU, a decoded simple_add bypass can regress because its extra EX operand/control muxing and duplicate adder fanout sit on the same forwarded-result/load-address cone CoreMark already stresses.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
