{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261003-002-r3s1/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md 2>/dev/null || true\"","aggregated_output":"One-entry store drain buffer implementation notes\n\nWhat changed:\n- Added a one-entry ordinary-store buffer inside `rtl/mem_stage.sv`.\n- Ordinary non-MMIO stores can retire into the buffer when `io_dmemReady` is low; the buffer drives the external dmem bus until a ready cycle accepts it.\n- Younger loads, MMIO stores, and FENCE wait behind a pending buffered store. EBREAK also waits if the buffer has not drained, so test-harness termination cannot drop a final buffered write.\n- CoreMark/UART marker MMIO stores in `0x10000000..0x100001ff` remain unbuffered and blocking.\n- Replaced the hazard unit's raw dmem stall inputs with a MEM-stage `memory_blocked` signal.\n- Extended `test/test_pipeline.py` with dmem-ready scheduling and directed coverage for buffered drain, store-load ordering, FENCE drain ordering, MMIO marker blocking, and no double retirement under load stalls.\n\nDeviations:\n- I kept the buffer local to `mem_stage.sv` instead of adding a separate `store_buffer.sv`; the queue is only one valid bit plus address/data/mask registers, and local ownership keeps the arbitration path easier to audit.\n- I updated the existing pipeline cocotb test file rather than adding `test_store_buffer.py`, so the shared mini core harness did not need to be duplicated.\n\nConcerns:\n- The buffer intentionally allows same-cycle dequeue/enqueue for ordinary stores when an older buffered store drains and the current store can retire into the just-freed entry. Loads and MMIO stores do not share that path because they need the bus for their own access.\n- Local `make cosim TARGET=bench` defaults to `NRET=2` in this checkout's Makefile build step even though `cores/bench/core.yaml` declares `nret: 1`; I reran it as `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`, matching the evaluator's nret-aware environment.\n\nLocal status:\n- Verilator lint: pass\n- Cocotb pipeline tests: pass\n- Formal: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed\n- Cosim: pass with `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
