{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r7s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r7s2\ntitle: \"Registered lookahead next-PC predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts found real CoreMark cycle savings from predicting hot loop backedges, but they repeatedly lost Fmax because opcode decode, immediate target adders, BTB tag checks, or RAS selection fed the same-cycle fetch PC update path. The current core's score is Fmax-sensitive enough that another predictor only makes sense if its lookup work is removed from that path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny direct-mapped lookahead next-PC predictor whose table lookup runs one cycle ahead of use. While fetching PC P, the predictor also looks up the next sequential fetch address P+4 and registers that entry's taken bit and target. On the following cycle, when P+4 is the fetched instruction, the IF PC update mux consumes only the registered prediction result, not a live tag compare or target calculation.\n\n  Train the predictor from EX-resolved direct conditional branches and JALs, with two-bit counters for conditional direction and stored aligned targets. Carry the registered predicted-taken bit and target through IF/ID and ID/EX so EX can suppress redirects on correct predictions and recover stale/aliased entries or loop exits by redirecting to the resolved next PC. This should keep the useful one-cycle-earlier loop-backedge redirect from the better predictor attempts while avoiding their critical fetch feedback cone; first fetches after redirects simply fall back to not-taken until the lookahead register is primed.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add predicted-taken and predicted-target metadata to IF/ID and ID/EX payloads so predictions travel with the fetched instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg_first.sv\n    description: \"Mirror the pipeline payload metadata changes for wildcard-ordered SystemVerilog builds.\"\n  - file: rtl/lookahead_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a small direct-mapped BTB/BHT with registered lookahead lookup results and EX-stage update inputs.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the registered lookahead prediction as a low-cost PC update option below EX redirects and stalls, and expose prediction metadata with the IF/ID payload.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch prediction metadata into ID/EX without adding decode-stage target computation or predictor table access.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Resolve predicted branches against actual next PC, suppress redirects on correct predictions, and repair misses, aliases, loop exits, and misaligned targets.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire predictor lookup/update, registered prediction metadata, and EX recovery signals while preserving the existing nret=1 top-level IO.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Ensure lookahead prediction consumption is blocked or held consistently under imem, dmem, load-use, and DIV/REM stalls.\"\n  - file: test/test_lookahead_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add directed cocotb coverage for predicted loop backedges, loop-exit recovery, alias/stale-target repair, redirect priority, and stall-held predictions.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
