{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r10s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r10s0\ntitle: \"Opcode-aware forwarding masks\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current accepted core is again limited by a short but stubborn path that\n  starts at the register file or MEM/WB metadata, passes through the forwarding\n  selects and EX operand muxes, and reaches the ALU/address-generation result.\n  Prior attempts that added prediction, extra execute stages, or new bypass\n  datapaths tended to lengthen nearby control cones enough to lose. A narrower\n  micro-optimization should attack the same hot operand path while preserving\n  the five-stage timing model and CoreMark cycle count.\nhypothesis: |\n  Teach the forwarding unit which decoded operands are actually consumed by the\n  instruction in EX, and suppress bypass comparisons and mux selection for\n  unused sources. For example, LUI/AUIPC/JAL do not need rs1 or rs2 forwarding,\n  I-type ALU/load/JALR uses rs1 but not rs2, stores and branches use both, and\n  OP-IMM shift instructions still only need rs1. This lets the EX operand muxes\n  settle to the ID/EX register value for dead operands instead of depending on\n  EX/MEM and MEM/WB rd/reg_write comparisons, reducing fanout from writeback\n  metadata and removing useless MEM/WB-to-ALU select logic from many CoreMark\n  instructions. Because the decoded use masks are carried in ID/EX and only\n  gate existing forwarding decisions, the pipeline depth, load-use interlock,\n  branch resolution point, memory protocol, RVFI retirement, and CoreMark IPC\n  should remain unchanged.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add compact rs1_used and rs2_used decode bits to the ID/EX payload so execute and forwarding can distinguish live operands from instruction-field noise.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg_first.sv\n    description: \"Mirror the new ID/EX operand-use bits for wildcard-ordered builds.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Derive and latch rs1_used/rs2_used from opcode and funct class alongside the existing decoded control signals.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Gate EX/MEM and MEM/WB rd comparisons and forwarding selects with the latched operand-use bits, defaulting unused operands to no-forward.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the ID/EX operand-use bits into the forwarding unit without changing the top-level nret=1 IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add directed dependency tests covering I-type, LUI/AUIPC/JAL, stores, branches, and load-use hazards so masked forwarding cannot hide a real RAW dependency.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
