{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r10s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r10s0\ntitle: \"Narrow ID/EX bubble kills\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current accepted core is again limited by a short but stubborn path that\n  starts around the register-file/ID boundary, passes through EX operand\n  delivery and the ALU, and lands in the EX/MEM or memory-address endpoint.\n  Earlier wins came from removing unnecessary work from nearby control cones,\n  while prediction, deeper execute staging, and extra bypass datapaths tended\n  to lose by adding muxes to the same region. The ID stage still turns every\n  flush or invalid fetch into a full-width zero assignment of the ID/EX bundle,\n  so redirect, imem_ready, and hazard control fan out into the 32-bit operand,\n  immediate, PC, and instruction fields even though an invalid entry will never\n  retire.\nhypothesis: |\n  Convert ID/EX bubble insertion from \"zero the whole pipeline payload\" into a\n  narrow side-effect kill. On reset the register can still clear fully, but on\n  flush or `!IF/ID.valid` the ID stage should only clear `valid` and the small\n  set of control bits that could cause redirects, memory requests, register\n  writes, or traps; the wide data fields may hold their previous value or latch\n  don't-care fetched bits because `valid=0` prevents retirement. This removes\n  EX redirect/imem/hazard decisions from the rs1/rs2/imm/pc/instr data muxes\n  feeding the current EX critical path, while preserving the five-stage\n  pipeline, load-use behavior, branch resolution point, dmem protocol, RVFI\n  ordering, and CoreMark cycle count. The implementation should keep invalid\n  entries side-effect-free either by clearing those decoded control bits in\n  ID/EX or by locally qualifying EX/MEM actions with `valid`, but it should not\n  add new predictor, scoreboard, or ALU bypass logic.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"On flush or invalid IF/ID input, clear only ID/EX valid plus side-effecting control bits instead of assigning zero to the full wide payload.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Audit redirect, long-operation start, and EX/MEM side-effect propagation so an ID/EX entry with valid=0 cannot redirect, start DIV/REM, write registers, or issue memory operations even if data fields are stale.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Keep dmem read/write enables and RVFI memory masks side-effect-free for invalid EX/MEM bubbles if control/data fields are no longer fully zeroed upstream.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add directed flush, imem-stall, redirect, and invalid-bubble tests that confirm stale held payload fields cannot cause redirects, memory requests, register writes, traps, or duplicate RVFI retirements.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
