{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r11s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r11s0\ntitle: \"Isolate single-cycle multiplier mux\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The accepted core is now limited by a short EX-stage path through forwarded\n  operands, the ALU, and the EX/MEM result or memory-address register. Prior\n  attempts show that making MUL multicycle hurts CoreMark, but the current ALU\n  still makes every ADD, branch compare companion path, and load/store address\n  share a result mux with the DSP-backed MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU cases.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep the existing single-cycle RV32M multiply latency, but move multiply\n  product generation and MUL result selection out of the main RV32I ALU case.\n  The ALU becomes an RV32I fast-result block for ADD/SUB/logic/shift/compare\n  and LUI, while EX computes the shared signed 33x33 product in parallel and\n  selects that product only for decoded MUL* operations. This should reduce the\n  hot ADD/load-address output mux and opcode-decode depth without adding stalls,\n  predictors, or new pipeline stages.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Remove real MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU product generation from the main ALU result case, leaving RV32I fast operations plus the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS stand-ins.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate the shared single-cycle multiplier product beside the ALU, choose its low/high result only for MUL* opcodes, and preserve existing DIV/REM long-stall handling.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Optionally add compact decoded MUL classification bits or helper constants so EX can select multiplier signedness without widening the critical RV32I ALU mux.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg_first.sv\n    description: \"Mirror any core_pkg helper declarations needed for wildcard-ordered builds.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Keep or extend focused MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU vectors so separating the multiplier from the ALU case cannot change RV32M bit results.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
