{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r13s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r13s0\ntitle: \"Mask load EX bypass\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The accepted micro-opt wins all came from shortening the hot EX operand to\n  ALU result cone, while recent attempts that added prediction, load bypassing,\n  or execute sideband control widened that same path.  The current forwarding\n  unit still treats every EX/MEM register-writing instruction as an immediately\n  bypassable source, including loads whose data is not available until MEM/WB.\n  Load-use interlocks already keep true consumers out of EX until the load has\n  advanced, so advertising EX/MEM loads to the forwarding mux is unnecessary\n  timed logic on the critical operand-select path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Qualify the EX/MEM forwarding source as bypassable only for valid non-load\n  register writers, leaving loads to forward exclusively from MEM/WB after the\n  existing one-cycle interlock and dmem-stall hold behavior.  This should remove\n  impossible load-address selections from the forwarding select cone and reduce\n  ALU operand mux pressure without adding a new datapath, changing CoreMark IPC,\n  or revisiting the source-qualified load-use optimization that previously\n  broke RVFI source capture.  Correctness is preserved because a load in EX/MEM\n  never has architectural rd data available for a younger EX-stage consumer.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Drive the EX/MEM forwarding write-enable with valid non-load register writes instead of raw ctrl.reg_write.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Treat the EX/MEM input as an already-qualified bypass-valid signal and keep MEM/WB forwarding priority unchanged.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add directed load-use, dmem-stall, and load-followed-by-false-source cases to confirm loads still forward only from MEM/WB.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
