{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_19", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20261003-001-r5s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20261003-001-r11s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20261003-001-r3s0\\\") | \\\"ID: \\\\(.id)\\\\nTITLE: \\\\(.title)\\\\nOUTCOME: \\\\(.outcome) fitness=\\\\(.fitness) delta=\\\\(.delta_pct) fmax=\\\\(.fmax_mhz) cycles=\\\\(.cycles) lut4=\\\\(.lut4) dsp=\\\\(.dsp)\\\\nCRIT: \\\\(.critical_path | tostring)\\\\nNOTES:\\\\n\\\\(.implementation_notes // \\\"\\\")\\\\nLESSON:\\\\n\\\\(.lesson // \\\"\\\")\\\\n---\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "ID: hyp-20261003-001-r3s0\nTITLE: Bypass full ALU for address adds\nOUTCOME: regression fitness=114.75 delta=-0.97 fmax=51.544 cycles=4491817 lut4=2743 dsp=6\nCRIT: {\"from\":\"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\",\"to\":\"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\",\"slack_ns\":-14.645,\"arrival_ns\":24.94,\"logic_cells\":13,\"modules\":[\"clock_ibuf\",\"cpu/u_id\",\"cpu/u_ex\",\"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\"cpu/u_ex\"]}\nNOTES:\nBypass full ALU for address adds\n\nChanged:\n- Added ctrl.simple_add to core_pkg.sv and mirrored it in 00_core_pkg_first.sv.\n- Decoder now asserts simple_add only for validated ADD, ADDI, LOAD, STORE, JAL, JALR, and AUIPC encodings. Illegal/default cases still leave it cleared.\n- ID stage carries the new decoded bit into the ID/EX control bundle.\n- EX stage now computes a forwarded fast_sum from the appropriate rs/pc and rs2/imm operands. ADD/ADDI/load/store/AUIPC results select fast_sum instead of the generic ALU output; branch, JAL, and JALR targets reuse the same narrow add path. JAL/JALR still write PC+4 as before.\n\nDeviations:\n- Kept ALU_ADD implemented inside alu.sv because the standalone ALU tests exercise it directly and the opcode remains a harmless compatibility/default value. The core datapath bypasses that result for decoded simple-add cases.\n- Did not add branch to ctrl.simple_add, since branch does not produce an architectural ALU result. Branch target arithmetic still uses the fast_sum path in EX.\n\nConcerns:\n- The added simple_add mux is intentionally small, but final benefit depends on Gowin's flattening and whether the new select is placed off the prior broad ALU result cone.\n\nLocal checks:\n- Verilator lint passed:\n  verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv\n- Formal passed with the nret=1 auto-detected wrapper:\n  RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh\n  Result: Formal: 53 passed, 0 failed.\n- Cosim passed with NRET=1, matching cores/bench/core.yaml:\n  NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench\n  Result: {\"passed\": true, \"elfs_tested\": 2}\n\nLESSON:\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-001-r3s0 (regression, -0.97%): After DIV/REM leave the ALU, a decoded simple_add bypass can regress because its extra EX operand/control muxing and duplicate adder fanout sit on the same forwarded-result/load-address cone CoreMark already stresses.\n---\nID: hyp-20261003-001-r5s0\nTITLE: Split dmem address from ALU result\nOUTCOME: regression fitness=124.51 delta=2.02 fmax=55.929 cycles=4491817 lut4=2723 dsp=2\nCRIT: {\"from\":\"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\",\"to\":\"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_0_s0\",\"slack_ns\":-12.73,\"arrival_ns\":23.024,\"logic_cells\":13,\"modules\":[\"clock_ibuf\",\"cpu/u_id\",\"cpu/u_ex\",\"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\"cpu/u_ex\"]}\nNOTES:\n\nLESSON:\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-001-r5s0 (regression, +2.02%): A dedicated EX/MEM mem_addr_result adder can regress once the full ALU result is no longer the binding dmem-address cost, because extra rs1/imm fanout, pipeline bits, and address routing outweigh the false-dependency removal.\n---\nID: hyp-20261003-001-r11s0\nTITLE: Isolate single-cycle multiplier mux\nOUTCOME: regression fitness=121.94 delta=-0.08 fmax=54.772 cycles=4491817 lut4=2710 dsp=2\nCRIT: {\"from\":\"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\",\"to\":\"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\",\"slack_ns\":-14.077,\"arrival_ns\":24.371,\"logic_cells\":13,\"modules\":[\"clock_ibuf\",\"cpu/u_id\",\"cpu/u_ex\"]}\nNOTES:\n\nLESSON:\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-001-r11s0 (regression, -0.08%): Pulling single-cycle MUL* selection out of the ALU did not improve CoreMark because the EX/MEM writeback path still needs an `is_mul_op ? mul_result : alu_result` mux and the multiplier continues to fan out from forwarded operands.\n---\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
