{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r14s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r14s0\ntitle: \"Narrow pipeline bubble clears\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current best designs are limited by the register-file/ID-to-EX ALU result cone, and recent attempts that added new prediction or forwarding sideband widened that same path.  Several stage registers still clear whole packed structs on reset, flush, invalid fetch, or DIV/REM busy bubbles even though the datapath fields are ignored whenever valid is low.  Those zero arms become extra mux inputs on hot operand and EX/MEM result flops without improving CoreMark IPC or correctness.\nhypothesis: |\n  Convert pipeline bubble/reset handling to clear only the valid bit and the small control fields that can cause side effects or redirects, while leaving wide data fields such as pc, rs values, immediates, ALU result, memory data, and RVFI-only payload fields as don't-care/held when the slot is invalid.  In ID/EX this keeps flush and invalid-fetch kills from muxing zeros onto rs/imm/pc data; in EX/MEM it removes the DIV/REM-in-progress zeroing arm from the hot ALU-result capture path; in MEM/WB it preserves the existing dmem-stall forwarding hold while clearing control on true bubbles.  Correctness is preserved because invalid slots do not retire, write registers, access memory, or redirect, and all real instruction captures still assign the full RVFI payload before valid is asserted.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"On reset, flush, and invalid IF/ID slots, clear only valid and the decoded control bundle needed to suppress side effects; avoid zeroing wide ID/EX datapath fields that are ignored while invalid.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace struct-wide EX/MEM bubble clears, especially during DIV/REM busy cycles, with narrow valid/control kills so the hot ALU-result and operand payload flops have fewer zero-mux arms.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Keep the dmem-stall MEM/WB hold behavior, but use narrow control/valid clearing for true bubbles and reset so invalid writeback slots cannot forward or retire while wide RVFI data is treated as don't-care.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add directed reset, redirect, invalid-fetch, dmem-stall, and DIV/REM-busy cases to confirm invalid slots never write registers, touch memory, redirect, or retire stale RVFI state.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
