{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r2s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r2s0\ntitle: \"Decouple fetch flush from hazard decode\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  After the iterative DIV/REM change, the measured worst path no longer runs\n  through the divider; it runs through the ID, EX redirect, IF flush, hazard,\n  and ID/EX capture-control cone. The current IF stage rewrites fetched\n  instruction bits to a NOP on flush so the hazard unit sees harmless register\n  numbers. That makes a control decision from EX feed back through IF into\n  load-use detection and then into the ID/EX register mux, which is exactly the\n  new timing bottleneck.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep fetched instruction bits independent of hazard-produced flush control and\n  use explicit valid gating instead. Have IF report valid directly from\n  imem_ready and redirect state, have ID latch a zero-control bubble whenever\n  IF/ID is invalid, and have the hazard unit qualify load-use detection with\n  both IF/ID.valid and ID/EX.valid. This should remove the IF instruction-NOP\n  feedback from the ID/EX enable/data path, shorten the current critical cone,\n  and preserve architectural behavior because invalid pipeline entries already\n  must not retire or trigger memory/register side effects.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Stop feeding hazard-produced flush back into the fetched instruction bits; drive IF/ID.valid from imem_ready and redirect while leaving instruction data raw.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"When IF/ID.valid is low, latch a zero-control bubble so invalid fetched bits cannot create false memory, writeback, branch, or hazard state.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Qualify load-use detection with IF/ID.valid and ID/EX.valid so wrong-path or stalled fetch data cannot request a bubble.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the new valid-qualified hazard inputs and pass imem_ready to IF without changing the top-level core IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add or adjust focused stall/redirect tests to cover imem stalls, taken redirects, and load-use hazards with the explicit-valid scheme.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
