{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r3s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r3s0\ntitle: \"Bypass full ALU for address adds\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion already removed the combinational divider and the\n  remaining Gowin path is a short but hot cone from register data through\n  forwarding, EX operand selection, and the ALU. CoreMark spends many cycles\n  on loads, stores, ADDI-style pointer bumps, and AUIPC/JAL address arithmetic\n  that only need a 32-bit add, yet those results still traverse the generic\n  ALU result mux that also selects shifts, compares, logic, and DSP-backed\n  multiply results.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a dedicated EX fast-add path for instructions whose result is known to\n  be simple addition: load/store effective addresses, ADD/ADDI, AUIPC, and\n  branch or jump target sums where applicable. Keep the existing ALU for\n  non-add RV32I operations and single-cycle MUL/MULH, but have ex_stage select\n  the fast adder result directly for the common add/address cases before the\n  broad ALU operation mux. This should shave a few LUT levels from the current\n  regfile/forwarding-to-EX/MEM timing path without changing pipeline latency,\n  branch policy, RVFI ordering, or the iterative DIV/REM behavior that already\n  proved valuable.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a dedicated fast_sum datapath from the forwarded EX operands and use it for load/store addresses, ADD/ADDI, AUIPC, and PC-relative control-flow sums while preserving existing stall and redirect behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Trim the generic ALU add case so non-add operations keep using the existing combinational unit, while common add/address results can bypass its broad result-selection mux.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"If needed, add a small decoded control bit marking simple-add operations so ex_stage does not have to reconstruct the fast-path predicate from the full ALU opcode cone.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg_first.sv\n    description: \"Mirror any core_pkg.sv control-bundle field change for wildcard-ordered builds.\"\n  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n    description: \"Drive the optional simple-add control bit only for validated ADD, ADDI, AUIPC, load, store, JAL, and JALR encodings, leaving illegal-default behavior unchanged.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
