{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20261003-001-r3s0\\\") | {title, outcome, fitness, delta_pct, fmax_mhz, cycles, lut4, ff, dsp, critical_path, implementation_notes, changes} ' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"title\": \"Bypass full ALU for address adds\",\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"fitness\": 114.75,\n  \"delta_pct\": -0.97,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 51.544,\n  \"cycles\": 4491817,\n  \"lut4\": 2743,\n  \"ff\": 696,\n  \"dsp\": 6,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -14.645,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 24.94,\n    \"logic_cells\": 13,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"Bypass full ALU for address adds\\n\\nChanged:\\n- Added ctrl.simple_add to core_pkg.sv and mirrored it in 00_core_pkg_first.sv.\\n- Decoder now asserts simple_add only for validated ADD, ADDI, LOAD, STORE, JAL, JALR, and AUIPC encodings. Illegal/default cases still leave it cleared.\\n- ID stage carries the new decoded bit into the ID/EX control bundle.\\n- EX stage now computes a forwarded fast_sum from the appropriate rs/pc and rs2/imm operands. ADD/ADDI/load/store/AUIPC results select fast_sum instead of the generic ALU output; branch, JAL, and JALR targets reuse the same narrow add path. JAL/JALR still write PC+4 as before.\\n\\nDeviations:\\n- Kept ALU_ADD implemented inside alu.sv because the standalone ALU tests exercise it directly and the opcode remains a harmless compatibility/default value. The core datapath bypasses that result for decoded simple-add cases.\\n- Did not add branch to ctrl.simple_add, since branch does not produce an architectural ALU result. Branch target arithmetic still uses the fast_sum path in EX.\\n\\nConcerns:\\n- The added simple_add mux is intentionally small, but final benefit depends on Gowin's flattening and whether the new select is placed off the prior broad ALU result cone.\\n\\nLocal checks:\\n- Verilator lint passed:\\n  verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv\\n- Formal passed with the nret=1 auto-detected wrapper:\\n  RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh\\n  Result: Formal: 53 passed, 0 failed.\\n- Cosim passed with NRET=1, matching cores/bench/core.yaml:\\n  NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench\\n  Result: {\\\"passed\\\": true, \\\"elfs_tested\\\": 2}\\n\",\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Add a dedicated fast_sum datapath from the forwarded EX operands and use it for load/store addresses, ADD/ADDI, AUIPC, and PC-relative control-flow sums while preserving existing stall and redirect behavior.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Trim the generic ALU add case so non-add operations keep using the existing combinational unit, while common add/address results can bypass its broad result-selection mux.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"If needed, add a small decoded control bit marking simple-add operations so ex_stage does not have to reconstruct the fast-path predicate from the full ALU opcode cone.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/00_core_pkg_first.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Mirror any core_pkg.sv control-bundle field change for wildcard-ordered builds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Drive the optional simple-add control bit only for validated ADD, ADDI, AUIPC, load, store, JAL, and JALR encodings, leaving illegal-default behavior unchanged.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
