{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r5s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r5s0\ntitle: \"Split dmem address from ALU result\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion's worst path still runs from the ID/EX operand side through the EX ALU cone to the dmem side of the FPGA wrapper. Prior attempts show that predictors, fetch queues, and broad simple-add bypasses lose when they add muxing to sensitive paths, while the winning micro-opts removed unnecessary arithmetic fanout from the existing critical cone. The dmem address endpoint is currently driven by the generic EX/MEM alu_result field, so static timing can still see the multiply-capable ALU result network on a path that only load/store address generation actually needs.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a separate EX/MEM mem_addr_result field produced by a narrow rs1+imm adder for loads and stores, and drive mem_stage.dmem_addr and RVFI memory-address alignment from that field instead of from EX/MEM.alu_result. Keep alu_result as the ordinary writeback result for ADD/ADDI/AUIPC/JAL/MUL/etc., and avoid adding a new general-purpose simple-add result mux. This should remove the false dmem-address dependency on the full ALU case tree and shared RV32M multiplier output, while preserving load/store cycle timing, forwarding behavior, byte-lane masks, misalignment traps, and the nret=1 top-level contract.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a mem_addr_result field to ex_mem_t so the memory bus address has its own narrow producer instead of reusing the generic ALU result.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg_first.sv\n    description: \"Mirror the ex_mem_t field addition for wildcard-ordered builds that rely on the alphabetically first typedef shim.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute mem_addr_result from the forwarded rs1 operand plus the decoded immediate for load/store instructions, while leaving alu_result generation unchanged for writeback operations.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use in.mem_addr_result for dmem_addr, byte-lane mask placement, load extraction, misalignment checks, and aligned RVFI mem_addr instead of using in.alu_result.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add or preserve directed coverage for forwarded load/store addresses, misaligned traps, stalls, and byte/halfword lane selection so the split address path matches the old behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
