{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r6s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r6s0\ntitle: \"Move MULH variants off fast ALU\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current best core is again limited by the short ID/EX-to-ALU-to-EX/MEM cone.\n  Prior micro-opts show that broad bypasses and separate AGUs add too much muxing,\n  while reducing RV32M arithmetic fanout without changing hot single-cycle MUL was\n  just large enough to beat the acceptance threshold. The remaining shared 33x33\n  multiplier still feeds the common ALU result mux for MULH/MULHU/MULHSU even\n  though CoreMark C code is expected to be dominated by low-half MUL and RV32I\n  address/add/logic operations.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep ALU_MUL as a single-cycle low-half multiply, because making all multiply\n  operations multicycle already regressed, but move only MULH/MULHU/MULHSU onto\n  a small iterative high-half multiply unit that uses the existing EX long-stall\n  protocol. This lets alu.sv replace the always-present signed 33x33 product with\n  the cheaper low-half MUL datapath on the fast path and removes the high-half\n  product choices from the ordinary ALU output mux. If CoreMark rarely executes\n  high-half multiply, the Fmax gain from a simpler EX arithmetic cone should\n  outweigh the occasional long-op stall while preserving exact RV32IM behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Keep RV32I operations and ALU_MUL combinational, but remove real MULH/MULHU/MULHSU high-half products from the fast ALU result mux while preserving RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutions.\"\n  - file: rtl/mulh_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add an iterative signedness-aware high-half multiply unit for MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU, producing exact RV32M results without a single-cycle 33x33 product on the fast path.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Start the high-half multiply unit for MULH/MULHU/MULHSU, OR its busy/done sequencing into the existing long_stall path, and capture the completed result into EX/MEM exactly once.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Preserve or extend MULH/MULHU/MULHSU signed and unsigned corner vectors so the new iterative high-half path is checked against RV32M bit semantics.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
