{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r10s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-002-r10s1\ntitle: \"Bypassed split execute stage\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The best structural attempt so far split execute into operand-capture and ALU\n  stages, raising median Fmax to about 63 MHz, but it lost too many CoreMark\n  cycles to extra dependency and branch latency. The later scoreboarded version\n  fixed correctness conservatively and over-stalled dependent chains, giving up\n  the timing win. A narrower split with an explicit next-cycle result bypass can\n  target the same Fmax upside while recovering enough IPC to clear the acceptance\n  threshold.\nhypothesis: |\n  Restructure execute into EX0 and EX1, but treat the EX1 ALU result as a\n  first-class bypass source into EX0 operand capture instead of scoreboarding\n  every EX1 producer as unavailable. EX0 performs forwarding selection and\n  captures operands for EX1; when the previous instruction's EX1 result is the\n  freshest value, EX0 forwards that registered-stage result directly into the\n  next instruction's operand registers. Independent branches and JAL/JALR can\n  still redirect from EX0 using available operands, while branches that need an\n  unresolved EX1 value fall back to the late EX1 redirect path. This preserves\n  in-order RVFI retirement and avoids adding predictor or fetch-PC lookup logic,\n  but should recover a meaningful fraction of the cycles lost by the prior\n  split while keeping the ALU input boundary that improved Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add compact EX0/EX1 payload metadata for operand-captured execute, including result-availability bits needed for the explicit EX1 bypass.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg_first.sv\n    description: \"Mirror the EX0/EX1 typedef additions so wildcard-ordered SystemVerilog builds still see the same declarations.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Split execute into EX0 operand capture and EX1 ALU/memory-result generation, add an EX1-result bypass into EX0 operands, and provide late redirect fallback for dependent control flow.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Extend forwarding selection with an EX1 result source and a precise stall request only for consumers that cannot safely use the EX1 bypass.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Integrate the split-execute stall and early/late redirect priorities with the existing load-use, dmem, imem, and DIV/REM hold logic.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the split execute stage, EX1 bypass metadata, and redirect fallback signals without changing the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add directed coverage for adjacent ALU dependencies, load/store address dependencies, branch dependencies that use or cannot use the EX1 bypass, and redirects under bus stalls.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
