{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20261003-001-r4s0\\\") | .hypothesis.hypothesis, \\\"---\\\", (.changes[] | .file + \\\": \\\" + .description), \\\"---\\\", (.critical_path|tostring), \\\"---\\\", (.lut4|tostring), (.ff|tostring), (.dsp|tostring), (.cycles|tostring)' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"Replace the three parallel RV32M multiply expressions in alu.sv with one\nshared 33x33 signed product. Sign-extend each operand according to the\nselected MULH/MULHU/MULHSU signedness, use product[31:0] for MUL, and use\nproduct[63:32] for the high-half operations. This preserves exact RV32M bit\nresults and the existing RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutions, but should reduce\nDSP usage, EX operand fanout, and placement pressure on the current critical\nALU cone without changing pipeline structure or CoreMark cycle count.\n\n---\nrtl/alu.sv: Collapse the three separate RV32M multiplier expressions into a single signed-extended 33x33 product shared by MUL, MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU while leaving DIV/REM on the existing iterative path.\ntest/test_alu.py: Keep or extend focused multiply vectors, especially signed/unsigned high-half corner cases, so the shared multiplier is checked against RV32M bit semantics.\n---\n{\"from\":\"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\",\"to\":\"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\",\"slack_ns\":-13.468,\"arrival_ns\":23.763,\"logic_cells\":13,\"modules\":[\"clock_ibuf\",\"cpu/u_id\",\"cpu/u_ex\",\"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\"cpu/u_ex\"]}\n---\n2633\n695\n2\n4491817\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
