{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_2", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n \\\"category: structural|\\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\": ?\\\\\\\"structural\\\\\\\"|structural\\\" cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl cores/bench/LESSONS.md schemas/hypothesis.schema.json\"", "aggregated_output": "schemas/hypothesis.schema.json:8:    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Split RV32M off the EX fast path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline timing report points through the forwarding muxes into EX and\\nthen through the monolithic combinational ALU. That ALU contains full 32-bit\\nmultiply, divide, and remainder operators even though ordinary RV32I ALU,\\nbranch, and address-generation operations dominate CoreMark cycles. The\\ncurrent structure pays the RV32M timing cost on every instruction.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline timing report points through the forwarding muxes into EX and\\nthen through the monolithic combinational ALU. That ALU contains full 32-bit\\nmultiply, divide, and remainder operators even though ordinary RV32I ALU,\\nbranch, and address-generation operations dominate CoreMark cycles. The\\ncurrent structure pays the RV32M timing cost on every instruction.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Restructure execute into a one-cycle RV32I fast path plus a decoupled RV32M\\nsidecar. ADD/SUB/logic/shift/compare, branches, jumps, and load/store address\\ngeneration continue to retire through the existing pipeline cadence, while\\nMUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU use a registered DSP-backed result path and DIV/REM use\\nan iterative unit that stalls the front of the pipeline only while an M op is\\nactive. Removing `/` and `%` from the combinational EX result mux should cut\\nthe reported 150-level ALU/forwarding path dramatically; CoreMark should gain\\nmuch more from Fmax than it loses from occasional multicycle M operations.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 35, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add execution control fields or small enums needed to distinguish fast ALU, registered multiply, and iterative divide/remainder sequencing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Reduce the combinational ALU to\n…[63611 of 66683 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f67f26c64d7871ba]…\n\"regression\", \"fitness\": 120.11, \"delta_pct\": -1.58, \"vs_baseline\": 891.01, \"fmax_mhz\": 51.906, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4321614, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2697, \"ff\": 695, \"seeds\": [50.322, 51.906, 51.906], \"perturbations\": [[0, 50.322, 14], [1, 51.906, 15], [2, 51.906, 15]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_1_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -14.872, \"arrival_ns\": 25.166, \"logic_cells\": 16, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 14, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T09:15:10.561667Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 11, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-002-r11s1 (regression, -1.58%): Ready-qualified MEM->EX load bypass can lose even with combinational dmem because the load-data source and ready/pending forwarding select widen the hot operand/branch cone more than CoreMark's adjacent load-use savings repay.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
