{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\"|category: structural|structural|split execute|EX0|EX1|unified|load-use|forward|branch|redirect|retime|register|pipeline' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Move DIV/REM off EX critical path\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline timing path runs from MEM/WB forwarding control through the EX\\noperand muxes into the ALU and reaches about 150 logic levels. The current\\nALU contains fully combinational RV32M divide and remainder operators, so even\\nordinary forwarded ADD/load-address operations share timing with the largest\\narithmetic cone. Removing the divider from the single-cycle EX path should\\nraise Fmax by far more than the acceptance threshold, while CoreMark is\\nexpected to execute few or no DIV/REM instructions in the measured loop.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline timing path runs from MEM/WB forwarding control through the EX\\noperand muxes into the ALU and reaches about 150 logic levels. The current\\nALU contains fully combinational RV32M divide and remainder operators, so even\\nordinary forwarded ADD/load-address operations share timing with the largest\\narithmetic cone. Removing the divider from the single-cycle EX path should\\nraise Fmax by far more than the acceptance threshold, while CoreMark is\\nexpected to execute few or no DIV/REM instructions in the measured loop.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU logic in the ALU with a small\\niterative divider/remainder unit that stalls the in-order pipeline only while\\none of those rare operations is in EX. Keep ADD/SUB/logic/shift/compare and\\nDSP-backed MUL/MULH operations single-cycle, and have EX/MEM capture the\\nDIV/REM result only on the unit's done pulse. This should cut the current\\nALU-forwarding critical path while preserving exact RV32M results and RVFI\\nretirement order.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 30, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational divide/remainder operators from the timed ALU path, leaving only single-cycle non-DIV arithmetic and the existing RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutions.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mdiv_unit.sv\", \"de\n…[191555 of 194627 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:07571c8e42928247]…\nsion\", \"fitness\": 115.09, \"delta_pct\": -5.69, \"vs_baseline\": 849.59, \"fmax_mhz\": 49.63, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4312308, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2982, \"ff\": 825, \"seeds\": [49.484, 49.63, 49.63], \"perturbations\": [[0, 49.484, 20], [1, 49.63, 22], [2, 49.63, 22]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/repair_valid_q_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -15.209, \"arrival_ns\": 25.503, \"logic_cells\": 59, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 20, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T09:31:57.632716Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 12, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r12s2 (regression, -5.69%): Late-verifying direct-target prediction avoids same-cycle EX confirmation, but carrying `pred_*` metadata plus EX repair/kill control still costs more timing and loop-exit penalty than CoreMark gains from the speculative backedge fetch.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
