{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r13s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-002-r13s1\ntitle: \"Move LSU address generation into ID\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion's timed path repeatedly ends at the FPGA dmem array and\n  still runs through the register-file read, EX forwarding muxes, and ALU add\n  cone. Prior attempts that duplicated the AGU inside EX only shifted this path\n  slightly, because memory addresses were still produced from the same\n  forwarded EX operand surface. Full EX splitting bought Fmax but lost too many\n  CoreMark cycles from extra branch and dependency latency.\nhypothesis: |\n  Restructure the load/store address path so memory effective addresses are\n  computed in ID, registered with the decoded instruction, and carried through\n  EX/MEM as a dedicated LSU address. The ID AGU should use the regfile value or\n  a small EX/MEM and MEM/WB writeback forward for rs1; only load/store\n  instructions whose base register is still unavailable in ID should interlock.\n  Store data and ordinary ALU operations keep the existing EX forwarding path,\n  so branch latency and ALU producer-consumer cadence are not globally\n  stretched.\n\n  This should remove the hot forwarded-rs1-to-ALU-to-dmem-address structure\n  for the common case where load/store bases are already in the register file\n  or forwardable from an older registered result. The expected cycle cost is\n  limited to true base-address RAW cases, while Fmax should improve because the\n  dmem address, mask, misalignment, and load-extract logic consume a registered\n  LSU address rather than the generic ALU result path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a dedicated load/store effective-address field to the ID/EX and EX/MEM payloads, plus any compact metadata needed to distinguish valid precomputed LSU addresses.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg_first.sv\n    description: \"Mirror the payload-field changes in the wildcard-order typedef shim.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate an ID-stage AGU for LOAD/STORE rs1+imm using regfile data or forwarded registered producer data, and latch the result with the decoded memory instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Provide a narrow ID-side base-register forwarding choice from EX/MEM ALU results and MEM/WB writeback data without changing the existing EX operand forwarding priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add a load/store base-address interlock for cases where ID cannot yet compute the correct rs1+imm address, while preserving current load-use, dmem, imem, redirect, and DIV/REM stall priorities.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Carry the precomputed LSU address into EX/MEM for memory operations, while continuing to use the normal ALU result for non-memory writeback and branch/jump handling.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Drive dmem address, byte mask generation, misalignment checks, load extraction, and RVFI memory address fields from the dedicated registered LSU address.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the ID AGU forwarding and base-interlock signals between ID, forwarding, hazard, EX, and MEM without changing the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add directed tests for load/store bases from regfile, EX/MEM forward, MEM/WB forward, unavailable ALU producers, unavailable load producers, dmem stalls, and misaligned memory traps.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
