{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r14s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-002-r14s1\ntitle: \"Stall-fill fetch skid buffer\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current best core still pays independent random instruction-memory stalls\n  after cycles where the pipeline was already frozen by dmem backpressure or a\n  long EX operation. Prior full IF queues and predictors lost because they put\n  counters, target muxes, or prediction metadata on the normal fetch/decode\n  path. A narrower structure can exploit the same stalled-PC situation without\n  changing the fall-through PC path or speculating ahead.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a one-entry fetch skid buffer that only fills while the PC is held for a\n  non-fetch stall and io_imemReady is high. When the back-end stall releases,\n  the buffered instruction for the held PC is supplied to ID even if the next\n  io_imemReady sample is low, then the buffer is consumed as the PC advances.\n  Redirects clear the buffer, and the design never fetches beyond the current\n  PC, so branch recovery, RVFI order, and memory-side behavior stay aligned\n  with the existing single-issue pipeline. This should recover cycles by\n  overlapping a fraction of the 22 percent imem stalls with dmem stalls while\n  adding only a small same-PC instruction/valid mux, not a predictor or queue\n  counter on the critical PC feedback path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-entry same-PC instruction skid buffer that fills during non-fetch pipeline stalls, supplies buffered instructions after release, and clears on redirect or reset.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Replace raw io_imemReady front-end stalling with an IF-supply-ready signal so a buffered instruction can let the pipeline advance when memory is not ready.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the IF skid-buffer availability signal between fetch and hazard logic without changing the top-level nret=1 IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_fetch_skid.py\n    description: \"Add directed coverage for dmem-stall/imem-ready fill, post-stall imem-not-ready consume, redirect clearing, and no double-retirement under held PC conditions.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
