{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r2s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-002-r2s1\ntitle: \"Register the IF/ID boundary\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current best design has already removed the enormous combinational divider path, and the new worst timing path is no longer arithmetic dominated. Gowin reports a feedback-shaped path from the register file and ID logic through EX redirect, IF flush generation, the hazard unit, and back into the ID/EX register controls. The existing front end has no real IF/ID register, so instruction bits, valid, redirect, imem backpressure, load-use detection, and ID/EX enable/flush selection all share one same-cycle control cone.\nhypothesis: |\n  Convert the combinational IF/ID boundary into a real registered fetch/decode boundary with explicit valid, hold, and flush behavior. Let IF own a small IF/ID register that captures pc/instruction only when imem is ready, holds through downstream stalls, and clears on redirects; let ID and the hazard unit consume only the registered instruction metadata. This should break the current EX-to-IF-to-hazard-to-ID feedback timing path and allow Fmax to rise well beyond the branch/fetch latency cost. The design remains single-retire RV32IM and keeps DIV/REM iterative while preserving the top-level nret=1 RVFI contract.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 12\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Adjust the IF/ID payload comments or fields if needed so the bundle represents a clocked valid fetch slot rather than a purely combinational view.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a registered IF/ID slot with hold-on-stall, capture-on-imem-ready, and redirect/flush invalidation while keeping the PC redirect priority correct.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Retune stall and flush outputs for a registered IF/ID boundary so load-use, imem stall, dmem stall, long EX ops, and redirects no longer form a same-cycle loop back into ID.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Decode and read registers from the registered IF/ID instruction and preserve the existing ID/EX bubble and hold behavior under the revised control semantics.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the revised fetch/decode hold and flush controls without changing the top-level memory or RVFI ports.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
