{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r4s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-002-r4s1\ntitle: \"Add a fall-through fetch queue\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion is no longer dominated by the old divider path; its\n  remaining gains must come from either small timing improvements or hiding the\n  benchmark's random bus stalls. Prior predictor and store-buffer attempts\n  added logic to sensitive IF/EX or dmem paths and regressed, but the core still\n  discards useful fetch opportunities whenever load-use, dmem, or long EX stalls\n  hold decode while imem happens to be ready.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the current PC-hold-only fetch stage with a tiny fall-through\n  instruction queue, ideally two entries deep. When decode is ready and the\n  queue is empty, fetched instructions still bypass directly to ID so the\n  zero-stall path keeps its current latency. When decode is blocked by load-use,\n  dmem backpressure, or DIV/REM, IF keeps accepting ready imem beats until the\n  queue fills; when imem later stalls, ID can drain queued instructions instead\n  of injecting bubbles. Taken redirects flush the queue and restart fetch from\n  the resolved target. This should recover a meaningful fraction of CoreMark's\n  22% iStall cost without adding branch prediction, dmem arbitration, or a new\n  ALU result mux on the known critical cones.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Turn IF into a fall-through two-entry instruction queue with fetch PC, queued PC/instruction/valid state, decode-consume control, redirect flush, and direct bypass when empty.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Remove raw imem_ready as a global stall reason; drive decode bubbles from IF/queue valid while allowing fetch to continue during backend stalls until the queue is full.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire decode-consume and fetch-queue-full/valid signals between IF and the existing hazard/decode path without changing the top-level IO or nret=1 RVFI contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_fetch_queue.py\n    description: \"Add directed cocotb coverage for imem stalls hidden by queued instructions, load-use stalls preserving the queued instruction, dmem stalls filling then draining the queue, and redirect flush behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
