{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r6s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-002-r6s1\ntitle: \"Register decode-time forwarding selects\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current best core is again limited by the ID/EX-to-ALU region, and the\n  recent structural attempts that added queues, predictors, store arbitration,\n  or duplicate address adders all paid for extra muxing on sensitive paths.\n  One remaining structural cone is the same-cycle forwarding compare path:\n  ID/EX source register numbers are compared against the older pipeline\n  destinations, then those selects immediately drive the EX operand muxes and\n  the ALU result register. That work is predictable one cycle earlier when the\n  instruction is still in decode.\nhypothesis: |\n  Move forwarding selection from EX-time combinational compare logic into the\n  decode-to-execute pipeline boundary. While an instruction is in IF/ID, compare\n  its rs1/rs2 against the current ID/EX and EX/MEM destination registers, using\n  those stages as the values that will become EX/MEM and MEM/WB when the\n  decoded instruction reaches EX. Latch the two forwarding select fields into\n  id_ex_t and have EX use the registered selects directly.\n\n  This keeps the existing ALU operand muxing and all single-cycle producer to\n  consumer behavior, but removes the register-number comparator and priority\n  logic from the EX critical path. Load-use stalls, dmem holds, and DIV/REM\n  long stalls should preserve correctness because the select bits travel with\n  the held ID/EX instruction, and load-use replay recomputes the select after\n  the load advances to the MEM/WB forwarding position.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add fwd_rs1_sel and fwd_rs2_sel fields to id_ex_t so forwarding choices are registered with the decoded instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg_first.sv\n    description: \"Mirror the id_ex_t forwarding-select fields for wildcard-ordered builds.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Retarget the existing priority comparator for decode-time use, comparing IF/ID rs fields against the current ID/EX and EX/MEM writer metadata.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Accept decode-time forwarding select inputs and latch them into ID/EX alongside rs values, immediates, control, and register addresses.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the registered forwarding selects from id_ex_t instead of same-cycle forward_unit outputs for the rs1 and rs2 operand muxes.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the forwarding unit before ID/EX capture and remove the EX-stage forwarding-select wires from the critical path without changing top-level IO.\"\n  - file: test/test_forwarding.py\n    description: \"Add directed coverage for ALU-to-ALU, load-use replay, store-data, dmem-stall hold, and DIV/REM-stall interactions with registered forwarding selects.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
