{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20261003-001-r4s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20261003-001-r5s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20261003-002-r5s1\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20261003-002-r6s1\\\") | {id,title,category,outcome,fitness,delta_pct,fmax_mhz,cycles,lut4,ff,dsp,critical_path,hypothesis:.hypothesis.hypothesis,notes:.implementation_notes} | @json' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\":\"hyp-20261003-001-r4s0\",\"title\":\"Share RV32M multiply datapath\",\"category\":\"micro_opt\",\"outcome\":\"improvement\",\"fitness\":122.04,\"delta_pct\":5.32,\"fmax_mhz\":54.816,\"cycles\":4491817,\"lut4\":2633,\"ff\":695,\"dsp\":2,\"critical_path\":{\"from\":\"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\",\"to\":\"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\",\"slack_ns\":-13.468,\"arrival_ns\":23.763,\"logic_cells\":13,\"modules\":[\"clock_ibuf\",\"cpu/u_id\",\"cpu/u_ex\",\"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\"cpu/u_ex\"]},\"hypothesis\":\"Replace the three parallel RV32M multiply expressions in alu.sv with one\\nshared 33x33 signed product. Sign-extend each operand according to the\\nselected MULH/MULHU/MULHSU signedness, use product[31:0] for MUL, and use\\nproduct[63:32] for the high-half operations. This preserves exact RV32M bit\\nresults and the existing RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutions, but should reduce\\nDSP usage, EX operand fanout, and placement pressure on the current critical\\nALU cone without changing pipeline structure or CoreMark cycle count.\\n\",\"notes\":\"\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20261003-001-r5s0\",\"title\":\"Split dmem address from ALU result\",\"category\":\"micro_opt\",\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"fitness\":124.51,\"delta_pct\":2.02,\"fmax_mhz\":55.929,\"cycles\":4491817,\"lut4\":2723,\"ff\":727,\"dsp\":2,\"critical_path\":{\"from\":\"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\",\"to\":\"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_0_s0\",\"slack_ns\":-12.73,\"arrival_ns\":23.024,\"logic_cells\":13,\"modules\":[\"clock_ibuf\",\"cpu/u_id\",\"cpu/u_ex\",\"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\"cpu/u_ex\"]},\"hypothesis\":\"Add a separate EX/MEM mem_addr_result field produced by a narrow rs1+imm adder for loads and stores, and drive mem_stage.dmem_addr and RVFI memory-address alignment from that field instead of from EX/MEM.alu_result. Keep alu_result as the ordinary writeback result for ADD/ADDI/AUIPC/JAL/MUL/etc., and avoid adding a new general-purpose simple-add result mux. This should remove the false dmem-address dependency on the full ALU case tree and shared RV32M multiplier output, while preserving load/store cycle timing, forwarding behavior, byte-lane masks, misalignment traps, and the nret=1 top-level contract.\\n\",\"n\n…[1581 of 4653 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:dbc4e77172e45c42]…\n7,\"arrival_ns\":24.651,\"logic_cells\":12,\"modules\":[\"clock_ibuf\",\"cpu/u_id\",\"cpu/u_ex\",\"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\"cpu/u_ex\"]},\"hypothesis\":\"Move forwarding selection from EX-time combinational compare logic into the\\ndecode-to-execute pipeline boundary. While an instruction is in IF/ID, compare\\nits rs1/rs2 against the current ID/EX and EX/MEM destination registers, using\\nthose stages as the values that will become EX/MEM and MEM/WB when the\\ndecoded instruction reaches EX. Latch the two forwarding select fields into\\nid_ex_t and have EX use the registered selects directly.\\n\\nThis keeps the existing ALU operand muxing and all single-cycle producer to\\nconsumer behavior, but removes the register-number comparator and priority\\nlogic from the EX critical path. Load-use stalls, dmem holds, and DIV/REM\\nlong stalls should preserve correctness because the select bits travel with\\nthe held ID/EX instruction, and load-use replay recomputes the select after\\nthe load advances to the MEM/WB forwarding position.\\n\",\"notes\":\"\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
