{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r8s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-002-r8s1\ntitle: \"Split EX with early redirects\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The closest structural attempt split EX into operand capture and ALU stages.\n  It lifted median Fmax from about 54.8 MHz to 63.5 MHz, but CoreMark cycles\n  grew from about 4.49M to 5.12M because every taken branch, jump, load-use\n  replay, and dependent ALU chain saw the deeper execute pipe. That result says\n  the timing headroom is real, but the split must not move hot control-flow\n  redirects later.\nhypothesis: |\n  Restructure execute into an early-control EX0 stage followed by a registered\n  data EX1 stage. EX0 performs the forwarding operand muxes and immediately\n  resolves BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU, JAL, and JALR redirect targets using the\n  selected operands. The resolved next PC, branch-taken bit, and any\n  misaligned-target trap metadata are carried into EX1 for retirement/RVFI, but\n  the frontend is redirected from EX0 in the same cycle as the current five-stage\n  core.\n\n  EX1 uses the EX0-registered operands for the existing ALU, MUL, DIV/REM\n  sequencing, load/store address generation, and EX/MEM payload. This keeps the\n  long regfile/forwarding-to-ALU path split roughly where the prior EX split\n  found Fmax, while recovering most CoreMark loop and jump IPC lost by moving\n  redirects a cycle later. Load-use hazards and true ALU result dependencies may\n  still pay the deeper data pipe, but taken control flow should return to the\n  old penalty without adding predictor tables or fetch-side target adders.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add an EX0-to-EX1 payload that carries forwarded operands, PC, immediate, destination/control metadata, resolved next-PC information, and trap bits.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg_first.sv\n    description: \"Mirror the new EX0-to-EX1 payload typedef so wildcard-ordered SystemVerilog builds keep compiling.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Split execute into EX0 early branch/jump resolution plus EX1 registered-operand ALU, mdiv, memory-address, and EX/MEM generation.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Provide forwarding choices for operands consumed in EX0, including the added EX1 producer state and existing EX/MEM and MEM/WB sources.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Update load-use, dmem-stall, long-DIV, and redirect flush/hold rules so early EX0 redirects kill only younger stages and never double-retire.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the refined execute split, early redirect signal, added forwarding sources, and revised stall controls without changing the nret=1 top-level IO.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add directed coverage for early EX0 branch/JAL/JALR redirects, redirect priority under stalls, EX1 ALU forwarding chains, load-use replay, and DIV/REM long stalls.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
