{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r9s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-002-r9s1\ntitle: \"Scoreboarded early-control EX split\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The most promising structural result so far was the EX0/EX1 split: it raised\n  median Fmax to about 63.5 MHz by registering operands before the ALU, but its\n  deeper execute pipe cost enough CoreMark cycles that the net gain missed the\n  acceptance threshold. The follow-up early-redirect split targeted that lost\n  IPC, but failed formal because RAW handling across the new EX1 producer was\n  incomplete.\nhypothesis: |\n  Rebuild the EX split as a scoreboarded early-control pipeline. EX0 performs\n  forwarding, captures operands into EX1, and resolves branch/JAL/JALR redirects\n  in the same cycle as the current five-stage core when operands are available.\n  A small producer scoreboard treats EX1, EX/MEM, and MEM/WB as distinct\n  availability points: consumers may forward from registered EX/MEM and MEM/WB,\n  but must interlock for an EX1 producer unless an explicitly timed bypass is\n  proven safe. This preserves the Fmax benefit of the registered ALU operand\n  boundary while recovering most taken-control-flow bubbles and preventing the\n  stale-rs RVFI failures seen in the prior early-redirect attempt.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add EX0/EX1 payload and compact producer-availability metadata for the split execute pipeline.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg_first.sv\n    description: \"Mirror the new payload typedefs and metadata so wildcard-ordered builds remain valid.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Split execute into EX0 early redirect/operand capture and EX1 registered ALU, mdiv, and EX/MEM generation with conservative EX1 RAW interlocks.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Extend forwarding decisions to distinguish EX1, EX/MEM, and MEM/WB producers and request a stall when the only matching producer is not yet forwardable.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Integrate the EX1 RAW stall with existing load-use, dmem, redirect, and long-DIV hold/flush priority without double retirement.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the split execute stage, early redirect path, and new stall signals while preserving the nret=1 top-level IO.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add directed tests for adjacent ALU dependencies, branch dependencies, early redirect under stalls, load-use replay, and DIV/REM holds in the split pipeline.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
