{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_2", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'rg -n \"category: predictor|predictor|BTB|BHT|RAS|return|branch|redirect|loop\" cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Move DIV/REM off EX critical path\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline timing path runs from MEM/WB forwarding control through the EX\\noperand muxes into the ALU and reaches about 150 logic levels. The current\\nALU contains fully combinational RV32M divide and remainder operators, so even\\nordinary forwarded ADD/load-address operations share timing with the largest\\narithmetic cone. Removing the divider from the single-cycle EX path should\\nraise Fmax by far more than the acceptance threshold, while CoreMark is\\nexpected to execute few or no DIV/REM instructions in the measured loop.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline timing path runs from MEM/WB forwarding control through the EX\\noperand muxes into the ALU and reaches about 150 logic levels. The current\\nALU contains fully combinational RV32M divide and remainder operators, so even\\nordinary forwarded ADD/load-address operations share timing with the largest\\narithmetic cone. Removing the divider from the single-cycle EX path should\\nraise Fmax by far more than the acceptance threshold, while CoreMark is\\nexpected to execute few or no DIV/REM instructions in the measured loop.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU logic in the ALU with a small\\niterative divider/remainder unit that stalls the in-order pipeline only while\\none of those rare operations is in EX. Keep ADD/SUB/logic/shift/compare and\\nDSP-backed MUL/MULH operations single-cycle, and have EX/MEM capture the\\nDIV/REM result only on the unit's done pulse. This should cut the current\\nALU-forwarding critical path while preserving exact RV32M results and RVFI\\nretirement order.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 30, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational divide/remainder operators from the timed ALU path, leaving only single-cycle non-DIV arithmetic and the existing RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutions.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mdiv_unit.sv\", \"de\n…[128973 of 132045 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2363415871d9939e]…\nssion\", \"fitness\": 124.63, \"delta_pct\": 2.12, \"vs_baseline\": 928.3, \"fmax_mhz\": 51.917, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4165827, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2697, \"ff\": 696, \"seeds\": [52.961, 51.917, 51.917], \"perturbations\": [[0, 52.961, 14], [1, 51.917, 13], [2, 51.917, 13]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_2_dmem_2_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -13.882, \"arrival_ns\": 24.176, \"logic_cells\": 14, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 14, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T08:31:03.099996Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r9s2 (regression, +2.12%): Even zero-table same-cycle redirect folding regresses when redirect_fold_valid muxes the EX target onto imem_addr and IF/ID valid/flush control, because removing a taken bubble does not repay the added redirect-to-fetch/hazard timing.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
