cause decoder/imm_gen target add and alignment logic remain on the PC update path while CoreMark backedge bubbles save too little to repay that timing cost.\nhyp-20261003-003-r6s2\tDecode-stage learned target predictor\tregression\t-27.2%\t38.081\t4286200\t- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r6s2 (regression, -27.20%): Decode-stage learned BTB/BHT still sits on the PC feedback path when IF/ID is combinational; tag/counter/target lookup plus the decode_redirect mux cost more timing than CoreMark saves from one-cycle-earlier taken redirects.\nhyp-20261003-003-r7s2\tRegistered lookahead next-PC predictor\tregression\t-22.07%\t40.541\t4262877\t- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r7s2 (regression, -22.07%): Registered lookahead lookup does not make branch prediction free: the IF pred_taken/pred_target PC mux plus carried IF/ID-to-ID/EX prediction metadata and EX resolved_next_pc compare still add enough front-end/control timing cost that CoreMark backedge savings do not repay it.\nhyp-20261003-003-r8s2\tRedirect-fill branch target instruction cache\tregression\t-11.1%\t46.238\t4261986\t- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r8s2 (regression, -11.10%): Redirect-fill BTICs can still lose CoreMark even off the normal IF predictor path, because the EX redirect_pc/target tag check plus redirect_fill_valid gating and target+4/instr injection land on the redirect-to-ID/IF control cone they were meant to avoid.\nhyp-20261003-003-r9s2\tSame-cycle redirect target fetch\tregression\t2.12%\t51.917\t4165827\t- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r9s2 (regression, +2.12%): Even zero-table same-cycle redirect folding regresses when redirect_fold_valid muxes the EX target onto imem_addr and IF/ID valid/flush control, because removing a taken bubble does not repay the added redirect-to-fetch/hazard timing.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
