{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'rg -n \"predict|BTB|BHT|branch|redirect|RAS|return|loop|BTIC|fold\" cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Move DIV/REM off EX critical path\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline timing path runs from MEM/WB forwarding control through the EX\\noperand muxes into the ALU and reaches about 150 logic levels. The current\\nALU contains fully combinational RV32M divide and remainder operators, so even\\nordinary forwarded ADD/load-address operations share timing with the largest\\narithmetic cone. Removing the divider from the single-cycle EX path should\\nraise Fmax by far more than the acceptance threshold, while CoreMark is\\nexpected to execute few or no DIV/REM instructions in the measured loop.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline timing path runs from MEM/WB forwarding control through the EX\\noperand muxes into the ALU and reaches about 150 logic levels. The current\\nALU contains fully combinational RV32M divide and remainder operators, so even\\nordinary forwarded ADD/load-address operations share timing with the largest\\narithmetic cone. Removing the divider from the single-cycle EX path should\\nraise Fmax by far more than the acceptance threshold, while CoreMark is\\nexpected to execute few or no DIV/REM instructions in the measured loop.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU logic in the ALU with a small\\niterative divider/remainder unit that stalls the in-order pipeline only while\\none of those rare operations is in EX. Keep ADD/SUB/logic/shift/compare and\\nDSP-backed MUL/MULH operations single-cycle, and have EX/MEM capture the\\nDIV/REM result only on the unit's done pulse. This should cut the current\\nALU-forwarding critical path while preserving exact RV32M results and RVFI\\nretirement order.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 30, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational divide/remainder operators from the timed ALU path, leaving only single-cycle non-DIV arithmetic and the existing RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutions.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mdiv_unit.sv\", \"de\n…[166128 of 169200 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:48fc830deba8143f]…\negression\", \"fitness\": 120.74, \"delta_pct\": -1.07, \"vs_baseline\": 896.2, \"fmax_mhz\": 51.43, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4259618, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2901, \"ff\": 728, \"seeds\": [51.503, 51.43, 51.43], \"perturbations\": [[0, 51.503, 14], [1, 51.43, 15], [2, 51.43, 15]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -14.416, \"arrival_ns\": 24.711, \"logic_cells\": 14, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 14, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T09:12:45.894834Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 11, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r11s2 (regression, -1.07%): ID-sideband target prefetch still leaves `pred_confirm`/`pred_accept` tied to EX redirect, imem_ready, and IF/ID flush gating, so moving the direct target off the EX imem-address mux did not remove CoreMark's front-end feedback cost.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
