{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r12s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r12s2\ntitle: \"Late-verified direct target predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts show that CoreMark can benefit from removing taken\n  direct-branch bubbles, but the implementations that confirmed prediction in\n  the same cycle as EX resolution lost too much Fmax through redirect, imem,\n  and IF/ID flush gating. The best near-miss reduced cycles enough to almost\n  clear the tournament threshold, so the promising angle is to keep the target\n  fetch benefit while taking EX branch confirmation out of the target-accept\n  timing path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a statically biased direct-target predictor for JAL and backward\n  conditional branches that accepts the predicted target fetch without waiting\n  for same-cycle EX confirmation. ID computes and registers the direct target\n  and fall-through PC; on the next cycle IF uses that registered target as a\n  one-slot speculative fetch and marks the younger instruction as predicted.\n  EX resolves the older branch in parallel, but instead of feeding its result\n  into the same-cycle accept/flush decision it registers a late repair: if the\n  prediction was wrong or the target was misaligned, the speculative younger\n  instruction is killed before it can retire or perform memory/writeback, and\n  the PC redirects to the resolved fall-through or trap-linear PC.\n\n  This trades an extra penalty on rare loop exits for a much shorter predictor\n  fast path on common taken backedges. It should preserve most of the cycle\n  reduction seen in direct redirect folding while avoiding the pred_confirm and\n  redirect_fold_accept cone that hurt Fmax in the previous predictor attempts.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add prediction metadata to the pipeline payloads: predicted slot flag, predicted target, fall-through PC, and late-kill bookkeeping.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg_first.sv\n    description: \"Mirror the pipeline payload metadata changes in the wildcard-order typedef shim.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Detect direct JALs and backward conditional branches, compute pc+imm and pc+4, and latch prediction metadata only when ID/EX captures a real instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the registered predicted target for a one-slot speculative fetch, advance PC to target+4, and tag the fetched instruction without waiting for EX confirmation.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Resolve the predicted direct control flow, produce a registered late-mispredict repair target, and suppress side effects for killed speculative slots.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Integrate the late-kill and repair redirect with existing load-use, dmem, imem, and long-DIV stall priorities without adding same-cycle EX confirm gating to IF.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the prediction, late-kill, and repair signals between ID, IF, EX, and hazard while preserving the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_late_verified_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add directed tests for taken backward branches, loop exits, JAL, misaligned targets, imem/dmem stall fallback, and RVFI order/PC consistency.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
