{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_1", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'rg -n \"category: predictor|predictor|BTB|BHT|RAS|return|branch prediction|predict\" cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Static loop branch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current five-stage pipeline fetches linearly and redirects only after EX\\nresolves a taken branch or jump. CoreMark has many loop backedges, so the core\\nrepeatedly pays taken-branch flush bubbles even though those branches are easy\\nto predict from their immediate direction. The existing critical path is in the\\nEX ALU/forwarding logic, so a very small IF-side predictor has a chance to\\nimprove iterations per cycle without materially changing Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current five-stage pipeline fetches linearly and redirects only after EX\\nresolves a taken branch or jump. CoreMark has many loop backedges, so the core\\nrepeatedly pays taken-branch flush bubbles even though those branches are easy\\nto predict from their immediate direction. The existing critical path is in the\\nEX ALU/forwarding logic, so a very small IF-side predictor has a chance to\\nimprove iterations per cycle without materially changing Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a static control-flow predictor in IF: predict direct JAL as taken, predict\\nconditional branches with negative B-immediates as taken, and predict forward\\nconditional branches plus JALR as not taken. Carry the predicted next PC through\\nIF/ID and ID/EX, then have EX redirect and flush only when the resolved next PC\\ndiffers from the prediction. This should remove most loop-backedge penalties in\\nCoreMark while keeping predictor cost to a few immediate-decode gates and one\\nextra next-PC field in the pipeline payload.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\"