{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'hyp-20261003-003-r4s2|hyp-20261003-003-r8s2|hyp-20261003-003-r9s2|hyp-20261003-003-r10s2|hyp-20261003-003-r11s2|hyp-20261003-003-r12s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "13:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-003-r4s2\", \"title\": \"Single-entry loop target predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current champion still pays a redirect bubble on every taken loop\\nbranch, and prior predictor experiments showed that removing those bubbles\\ncan cut CoreMark cycles by roughly five percent. The failures were timing\\nfailures: static prediction decoded immediates and added targets in IF, a\\ntiny BTB/BHT added table/tag/counter logic, and the RAS added exact JALR\\ndecode plus speculative stack repair. A useful predictor for this core must\\ntherefore be much smaller than a conventional BTB and must avoid imem-data\\ndecode on the fetch next-PC path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current champion still pays a redirect bubble on every taken loop\\nbranch, and prior predictor experiments showed that removing those bubbles\\ncan cut CoreMark cycles by roughly five percent. The failures were timing\\nfailures: static prediction decoded immediates and added targets in IF, a\\ntiny BTB/BHT added table/tag/counter logic, and the RAS added exact JALR\\ndecode plus speculative stack repair. A useful predictor for this core must\\ntherefore be much smaller than a conventional BTB and must avoid imem-data\\ndecode on the fetch next-PC path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a one-entry learned loop-backedge target predictor. EX trains the entry\\nonly when a resolved conditional branch is taken to a lower aligned target;\\nIF predicts taken only when the current fetch PC matches the registered\\nlearned branch PC, selecting the registered target instead of pc+4. Carry a\\npredicted-taken bit and predicted next PC through