{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r13s2.yaml\"", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261003-003-r13s2\ntitle: \"Prechecked redirect-fill BTIC\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The strongest predictor results came from redirect folding, especially the registered direct-target fold, because they recovered real CoreMark cycles without a full IF-time BTB. They still missed the acceptance threshold because the redirect cycle carried imem address muxing, imem_ready acceptance, flush suppression, and sometimes tag or target checks on a sensitive front-end/control path. Earlier BTIC and learned-loop designs also showed that tag compares and prediction metadata must not sit in the same cycle as the fetch redirect.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny branch-target instruction cache for direct JAL and conditional branch targets, but precheck it before the redirect cycle. When a direct control-flow instruction enters ID/EX, use its PC and ID-computed pc+imm target to look up a one- or two-entry BTIC and latch hit plus cached target instruction in a narrow sideband aligned with EX. If EX later resolves that same direct branch or JAL as taken and aligned, a prechecked hit injects the cached target instruction as the IF/ID payload during the redirect cycle and advances the PC to target+4; if the sideband misses, the branch is not taken, a stall blocks acceptance, or the target is misaligned, fall back to the current redirect bubble.\n\n  Training happens only after an ordinary redirect miss: remember the redirecting PC and resolved direct target, then fill the cached instruction when the target instruction is actually fetched with io_imemReady high. This keeps direction prediction conservative and avoids BTB/BHT counters, carried predicted-next-PC metadata, same-cycle EX target lookup, and imem_ready-dependent target fetch acceptance. It should preserve most of the CoreMark loop-backedge savings from redirect folding while trimming the timing cost that capped the prior predictor attempts.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_fill_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a tiny direct-control BTIC with registered prelookup hit/instruction sideband and miss-driven fill state for immutable instruction memory.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add minimal direct-target and prechecked-BTIC sideband fields needed to align a cached target instruction with the EX-stage branch.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg_first.sv\n    description: \"Mirror the payload and sideband typedef additions for wildcard-ordered builds.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute direct pc+imm targets for JAL and conditional branches and initiate the BTIC precheck only when ID/EX captures a valid direct control-flow instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the registered direct target for aligned direct redirects, qualify cached-instruction injection only with the prechecked hit and resolved taken outcome, and leave JALR on the existing fallback path.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Accept a cached target instruction on a prechecked redirect-fill hit, emit it as the IF/ID payload for the target PC, and advance the PC to target+4 without depending on same-cycle target imem readiness.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Suppress the normal redirect bubble only for an accepted cached fill, preserving existing load-use, dmem, imem, and long-DIV priorities on all fallback paths.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the BTIC prelookup, fill, and cached-instruction redirect handshake through the existing single-retire pipeline without changing the top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_prechecked_btic.py\n    description: \"Add directed cocotb coverage for miss training, repeated taken-branch fills, loop exits, misaligned fallback, dmem/imem stall fallback, target+4 PC advance, and RVFI PC/order consistency.\"\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
