{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_1", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'rg -n \"predict|BTB|BHT|BTIC|branch|backward|redirect|return|RAS|fold\" cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Split RV32M off the EX fast path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline timing report points through the forwarding muxes into EX and\\nthen through the monolithic combinational ALU. That ALU contains full 32-bit\\nmultiply, divide, and remainder operators even though ordinary RV32I ALU,\\nbranch, and address-generation operations dominate CoreMark cycles. The\\ncurrent structure pays the RV32M timing cost on every instruction.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline timing report points through the forwarding muxes into EX and\\nthen through the monolithic combinational ALU. That ALU contains full 32-bit\\nmultiply, divide, and remainder operators even though ordinary RV32I ALU,\\nbranch, and address-generation operations dominate CoreMark cycles. The\\ncurrent structure pays the RV32M timing cost on every instruction.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Restructure execute into a one-cycle RV32I fast path plus a decoupled RV32M\\nsidecar. ADD/SUB/logic/shift/compare, branches, jumps, and load/store address\\ngeneration continue to retire through the existing pipeline cadence, while\\nMUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU use a registered DSP-backed result path and DIV/REM use\\nan iterative unit that stalls the front of the pipeline only while an M op is\\nactive. Removing `/` and `%` from the combinational EX result mux should cut\\nthe reported 150-level ALU/forwarding path dramatically; CoreMark should gain\\nmuch more from Fmax than it loses from occasional multicycle M operations.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 35, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add execution control fields or small enums needed to distinguish fast ALU, registered multiply, and iterative divide/remainder sequencing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Reduce the combinational ALU to RV32I fast-path operations and keep RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS behavior consistent for non-sidecar builds.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/muldiv_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a new RV32M sidec\n…[196179 of 199251 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9b036499d772c31c]…\n 36.672, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4204420, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3327, \"ff\": 1050, \"seeds\": [34.778, 36.672, 36.672], \"perturbations\": [[0, 34.778, 32], [1, 36.672, 32], [2, 36.672, 32]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.direct_target_next_31_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -23.754, \"arrival_ns\": 34.052, \"logic_cells\": 61, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_id/u_imm\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 32, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T10:02:43.800813Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 13, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r13s2 (regression, -28.53%): Prechecking BTIC hits in ID still regresses when `btic_*` sideband state, `redirect_fill_accept`, and IF/ID instruction injection remain tied to EX redirect and imem_ready control, so target-cache wins must remove the redirect-cycle acceptance cone too.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
