{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r2s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r2s2\ntitle: \"Tiny trained branch target predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current core still resolves all taken branches and jumps in EX, so loop\n  backedges in CoreMark inject redirect bubbles even though the same PCs repeat\n  many times. The previous static predictor showed that removing those bubbles\n  can reduce CoreMark cycles, but it put immediate decode and target arithmetic\n  directly on the IF next-PC path and destroyed Fmax. A predictor that learns\n  resolved targets and reuses registered targets should keep the timing cost\n  much lower.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a very small direct-mapped branch target buffer with 2-bit direction\n  counters, trained only from resolved EX-stage control-flow instructions.\n  IF predicts a non-linear next PC only on a tag hit with a taken counter, using\n  the stored target rather than recomputing B/J immediates in fetch. Carry the\n  predicted next PC through IF/ID and ID/EX, and have EX redirect only when the\n  resolved next PC differs from the prediction. This should recover most\n  repeated loop-backedge bubbles seen in CoreMark while avoiding the failed\n  static predictor's wide immediate-add path in IF.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add predicted-next-PC metadata to IF/ID and ID/EX payloads so EX can compare prediction against the resolved next PC.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg_first.sv\n    description: \"Mirror the core_pkg.sv pipeline payload metadata for wildcard-ordered tool invocations.\"\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a tiny direct-mapped BTB/BHT that predicts from stored targets and updates on resolved branches and jumps.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the BTB/BHT prediction for the next PC when it hits, while preserving redirect and stall priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch predicted next-PC metadata into ID/EX alongside the fetched instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute the resolved next PC for branches and jumps, report predictor update information, and redirect only on prediction mismatch.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire predictor lookup/update signals between IF, EX, and the new branch predictor without changing the top-level IO contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
