{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r3s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r3s2\ntitle: \"Return-address stack predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The prior predictor experiments proved that CoreMark has enough taken-control\n  bubbles to matter, but both broad predictors hurt Fmax by putting branch\n  target calculation or BTB/BHT lookup logic directly on the IF next-PC path.\n  A return predictor is a narrower control-flow predictor with a much cheaper\n  fetch-side decision: exact RET instruction detection plus a registered stack\n  target, with no immediate adder, tag RAM, or saturating counter lookup.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny return-address stack for the common RISC-V call/return convention.\n  Push pc+4 for direct calls that write x1 or x5, pop/predict only on exact\n  RET-like JALR encodings using x1 or x5 with rd=x0 and imm=0, and carry the\n  predicted next PC through the pipeline so EX can recover on underflow,\n  aliasing, unusual JALR forms, or wrong stack contents. This should remove the\n  taken-redirect bubble on hot CoreMark function returns while keeping the\n  predictor off the failed branch-immediate and BTB timing paths.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/return_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a small 2- or 4-entry return-address stack with push, pop, top, valid, and flush-safe speculative pop repair signals.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Detect exact RET-style JALR instruction words in fetch and select the registered RAS top as predicted next PC when valid, preserving redirect and stall priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry predicted-next-PC and return-predicted metadata in IF/ID and ID/EX so EX can verify and recover precisely.\"\n  - file: rtl/00_core_pkg_first.sv\n    description: \"Mirror the pipeline metadata additions for wildcard-ordered tool invocations.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Classify calls and returns, push resolved return addresses, verify predicted returns against the resolved JALR target, and request redirect only on mismatch.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the return predictor between IF and EX without changing the top-level memory or nret=1 RVFI interface.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
