th EX redirects retaining priority for branches, JALR, traps, and all precise recovery cases.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add an early-redirect flush input so IF/ID and ID/EX are killed once for a decode-predicted direct transfer without perturbing load-use, dmem stall, or DIV/REM stall behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Accept a redirect generated from ID as the same kind of next-PC update used by EX today, preserving reset, stall, and existing EX redirect priority.\"\n  - file: test/test_decode_redirect.py\n    description: \"Add focused cocotb coverage for JAL early redirect, unconditional branch early redirect, EX-priority conflicts, and no early redirect for conditional branches or JALR.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
