 prediction for the branch in EX, suppress redirects for correctly predicted taken backedges, and redirect to pc+4 only on predicted-taken loop exits.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the ID prediction redirect and EX recovery redirect to IF with EX taking priority, without changing the top-level memory or nret=1 RVFI interface.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Keep flush generation tied to EX recovery redirects only, and ensure load-use, dmem, imem, and DIV/REM stalls block ID predictions instead of advancing the PC underneath a held branch.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a separate ID-prediction PC update path that changes the next fetch address without marking the current IF/ID branch invalid; existing EX redirects still kill the current wrong-path payload.\"\n  - file: test/test_decode_branch_predict.py\n    description: \"Add focused cocotb coverage for predicted taken backedges, loop-exit fall-through repair, stall-gated predictions, EX redirect priority, and no prediction for forward branches, JAL, JALR, or misaligned targets.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
