{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\"|predictor' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Static loop branch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current five-stage pipeline fetches linearly and redirects only after EX\\nresolves a taken branch or jump. CoreMark has many loop backedges, so the core\\nrepeatedly pays taken-branch flush bubbles even though those branches are easy\\nto predict from their immediate direction. The existing critical path is in the\\nEX ALU/forwarding logic, so a very small IF-side predictor has a chance to\\nimprove iterations per cycle without materially changing Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current five-stage pipeline fetches linearly and redirects only after EX\\nresolves a taken branch or jump. CoreMark has many loop backedges, so the core\\nrepeatedly pays taken-branch flush bubbles even though those branches are easy\\nto predict from their immediate direction. The existing critical path is in the\\nEX ALU/forwarding logic, so a very small IF-side predictor has a chance to\\nimprove iterations per cycle without materially changing Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a static control-flow predictor in IF: predict direct JAL as taken, predict\\nconditional branches with negative B-immediates as taken, and predict forward\\nconditional branches plus JALR as not taken. Carry the predicted next PC through\\nIF/ID and ID/EX, then have EX redirect and flush only when the resolved next PC\\ndiffers from the prediction. This should remove most loop-backedge penalties in\\nCoreMark while keeping predictor cost to a few immediate-decode gates and one\\nextra next-PC field in the pipeline payload.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted next-PC fields to IF/ID and ID/EX payloads so branch recovery can compare prediction versus resolved next PC.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode fetched direct control-flow opcodes in IF, compute B/J immediates, and advance the PC to the predicted next PC instead of always \n…[67957 of 71029 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:567e46eebc4b9994]…\n_mhz\": 40.541, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4262877, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3331, \"ff\": 790, \"seeds\": [39.014, 40.541, 40.541], \"perturbations\": [[0, 39.014, 27], [1, 40.541, 25], [2, 40.541, 25]], \"lutram\": 22, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_1_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs1_val_0_s100\", \"slack_ns\": -20.632, \"arrival_ns\": 30.926, \"logic_cells\": 76, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 27, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T07:45:22.540644Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 7, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r7s2 (regression, -22.07%): Registered lookahead lookup does not make branch prediction free: the IF pred_taken/pred_target PC mux plus carried IF/ID-to-ID/EX prediction metadata and EX resolved_next_pc compare still add enough front-end/control timing cost that CoreMark backedge savings do not repay it.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
